Relevant columns and their possible usage for the task “ How many distinct users viewed the most frequently visited page during January 2021? ”

• event_date : restrict rows to 20210101 … 20210131 (January 2021)  
• event_name : keep only the GA4 event that represents a page view (usually ‘page_view’)  
• event_params : unpack to obtain the page identifier – commonly the key = 'page_location' (full URL) or 'page_title' (title)  
• user_pseudo_id : treat as the user identifier; count DISTINCT values to know how many users saw a page  
• _TABLE_SUFFIX (pseudo‑column when querying with wildcards) : lets us query all daily tables in one shot and still limit them to the January 2021 range  

Typical filter conditions  
  WHERE event_name = 'page_view'  
    AND _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20210101' AND '20210131'  

10 exploration → solution queries
(Each query is limited to 20 rows so it can be run safely. Replace **project.dataset** with the actual names shown below.)

```sql
-- 1.  List all GA4 event names that appear on one January day
SELECT DISTINCT event_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210101`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  Look at all parameter keys for a single page_view event record
SELECT ep.key, ep.value.string_value, ep.value.int_value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210101`,
UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
WHERE event_name = 'page_view'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
